  "summary": "US GPU cloud (Meshive, operated by Steppod, LLC) that runs GPU pods and serverless inference on machines hosts contribute; customers ask for a card and are matched to a host, and Meshive sets one rate per card, reviewed every two weeks. The pricing page prints an on-demand and a spot rate per GPU-hour for each card and calls them starting prices: vCPU and memory above an included amount and storage are billed apart, and the console's live rate varies by availability and region. Billed by the minute; no egress fees. The page names no tax.",
  "notes": "Static pricing page /pricing (server-rendered, no charset sent - read as UTF-8): catalog rows pp-catalog-row - name, tier, \"<N>GB\", On-demand \"$X/hr\", Spot \"$X/hr\", availability badge; key (name, VRAM GB) -> id; per_gpu, gpu_count 1, advertised_from (\"per-GPU starting prices\"), instance = name; on_demand and spot; USD; region null. Two A100 forms on one form-less id keep the cheaper. docs.meshive.ai/documentation/pricing/ prints the same rates to four decimals.",
